{
    "chapter_num": 1,
    "verses_count": 27,
    "paragraphs_list": [
        {
            "type": "section_header",
            "text": "Salutation"
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 1,
                    "num_str": "1",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "James, a servant of God and of the Lord Jesus Christ,"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "LINE_BREAK",
                            "text": "\n"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "To the twelve tribes in the Dispersion:"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "LINE_BREAK",
                            "text": "\n"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Greeting."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_header",
            "text": "Faith and Wisdom"
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 2,
                    "num_str": "2",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Count it all joy, my brethren, when you meet various trials, "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 3,
                    "num_str": "3",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "for you know that the testing of your faith produces steadfastness. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 4,
                    "num_str": "4",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And let steadfastness have its full effect, that you may be perfect and complete, lacking in nothing."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 5,
                    "num_str": "5",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "If any of you lacks wisdom, let him ask God, who gives to all men generously and without reproaching, and it will be given him. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 6,
                    "num_str": "6",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "But let him ask in faith, with no doubting, for he who doubts is like a wave of the sea that is driven and tossed by the wind. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 7,
                    "num_str": "7, 8",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "For that person must not suppose that a double-minded man, unstable in all his ways, will receive anything from the Lord."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_header",
            "text": "Poverty and Riches"
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 9,
                    "num_str": "9",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Let the lowly brother boast in his exaltation, "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 10,
                    "num_str": "10",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "and the rich in his humiliation, because like the flower of the grass he will pass away. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 11,
                    "num_str": "11",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "For the sun rises with its scorching heat and withers the grass; its flower falls, and its beauty perishes. So will the rich man fade away in the midst of his pursuits."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_header",
            "text": "Trial and Temptation"
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 12,
                    "num_str": "12",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Blessed is the man who endures trial, for when he has stood the test he will receive the crown of life which God has promised to those who love him. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 13,
                    "num_str": "13",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Let no one say when he is tempted, “I am tempted by God”; for God cannot be tempted with evil and he himself tempts no one; "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 14,
                    "num_str": "14",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "but each person is tempted when he is lured and enticed by his own desire. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 15,
                    "num_str": "15",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Then desire when it has conceived gives birth to sin; and sin when it is full-grown brings forth death."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 16,
                    "num_str": "16",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Do not be deceived, my beloved brethren. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 17,
                    "num_str": "17",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Every good endowment and every perfect gift is from above, coming down from the Father of lights with whom there is no variation or shadow due to change."
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Other ancient authorities read variation due to a shadow of turning"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 18,
                    "num_str": "18",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Of his own will he brought us forth by the word of truth that we should be a kind of first fruits of his creatures."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_header",
            "text": "Hearing and Doing the Word"
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 19,
                    "num_str": "19",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Know this, my beloved brethren. Let every man be quick to hear, slow to speak, slow to anger, "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 20,
                    "num_str": "20",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "for the anger of man does not work the righteousness of God. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 21,
                    "num_str": "21",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Therefore put away all filthiness and rank growth of wickedness and receive with meekness the implanted word, which is able to save your souls."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 22,
                    "num_str": "22",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "But be doers of the word, and not hearers only, deceiving yourselves. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 23,
                    "num_str": "23",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "For if any one is a hearer of the word and not a doer, he is like a man who observes his natural face in a mirror; "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 24,
                    "num_str": "24",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "for he observes himself and goes away and at once forgets what he was like. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 25,
                    "num_str": "25",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "But he who looks into the perfect law, the law of liberty, and perseveres, being no hearer that forgets but a doer that acts, he shall be blessed in his doing."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 26,
                    "num_str": "26",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "If any one thinks he is religious, and does not bridle his tongue but deceives his heart, this man’s religion is vain. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 27,
                    "num_str": "27",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Religion that is pure and undefiled before God and the Father is this: to visit orphans and widows in their affliction, and to keep oneself unstained from the world."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        }
    ]
}